    "**Insight:** Electricity access was already fairly high (mid-60s%) by the 1990s and grew steadily to over 88% by the 2020s. Internet usage, in contrast, started from almost 0% in the 1990s and only began accelerating from the 2010s onward, eventually approaching the level of electricity access. This gap illustrates that South Africa electrified well ahead of going online — the digital transition lagged the electrical one by roughly two decades."
